D4  Stefan-Boltzmann and Hawking evaporation (photons only, geometric cross section)
  [OK] int_0^oo x^3/(e^x - 1) dx = Gamma(4) zeta(4) = pi^4/15  (closed form and independent mpmath quadrature 6.49393940227)
  [OK] photon energy density u = (pi^2/15) T^4
  [OK] sigma = u/(4 T^4) = pi^2/60
  [OK] P = sigma A T^4 = 1/(15360 pi G^2 M^2)
  [OK] evaporation time t = 5120 pi G^2 M^3
  [OK] CONTROL C-D4a: sigma = pi^2/30 (wrong) gives lifetime 2560 pi and is rejected
  [OK] [bookkeeping] 15360 pi = 60 (8 pi)^4/((pi^2)(16 pi)):  60 = 4 x 15 from sigma=pi^2/60;  (8 pi)^4 from T^4;  pi^2 from sigma;  16 pi from A
  [OK] [numerology flag] 15360 pi = 32 pi x 480 and 5120 pi = 32 pi x 160 (a literal factor, not an origin; 15360 = 2^10 x 15, 5120 = 2^10 x 5)
      caveat: the coefficient is model-dependent (species content, greybody factors); it is not a fundamental constant of gravity.

